Start each headset where its adaptive rate settled last time (Y2Linux radio daemon).

AAC's adaptive rate (patch 0002) and libldac's ABR start at the top level and
step down when the link cannot carry it: a headset that always settles lower
dropped audio during the first seconds of every stream. The platform's radio
daemon (y2-radiod) learns from EncoderStats (patch 0001) where each headset
settled and keeps /run/y2/bt-start/<ADDRESS>-<CODEC> (one number, 0 = top);
the encoders start there (src/y2-start-level.h) and still climb back when the
link allows. AAC: the level of its CBR levels (only with --aac-abr on a CBR
stream); LDAC: the EQMID, never higher quality than configured, only with
--ldac-abr. SBC keeps starting at its configured bit-pool: its packets are
sized for it, a lower start would size them for less.

--- a/src/a2dp-aac.c
+++ b/src/a2dp-aac.c
@@ -39,6 +39,7 @@
 #include "shared/rt.h"
 #include "y2-aac-abr.h"
 #include "y2-codec-ceiling.h"
+#include "y2-start-level.h"
 
 static const struct a2dp_bit_mapping a2dp_aac_channels[] = {
 	{ AAC_CHANNEL_MODE_MONO, .ch = { 1, a2dp_channel_map_mono } },
@@ -172,6 +173,12 @@
 		bitrate = mtu_bitrate;
 	struct y2_aac_abr abr;
 	y2_aac_abr_init(&abr, bitrate, config.aac_abr, !configuration->vbr);
+	/* Y2: start where this headset settled last time (y2-start-level.h). */
+	if (abr.enabled) {
+		abr.level = (unsigned int)y2_start_level(&t->d->addr, "AAC", Y2_AAC_ABR_LEVELS);
+		abr.current = abr.rates[abr.level];
+		bitrate = abr.current;
+	}
 	unsigned int current_bitrate = bitrate;
 	/* PCM frames since the ceiling was last looked at: the first frame looks
 	 * (y2-codec-ceiling.h), then about once a second. */
